---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { correctionIssueUrl } from '../lib/site';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contribute"
  description="Suggest corrections and source improvements. Community contribution does not determine Catholic teaching."
>
  <section class="section-tight shell fade-in">
    <p class="eyebrow">✦ Contribute</p>
    <h1 class="h1">Help make the representation more accurate.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Catholic Context’s community layer is correction, sources, translations, and evals —
      not a perspective forum on the knowledge object. Votes do not determine doctrine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell prose">
    <h2 class="h2">Public corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone may suggest a correction. The form opens a structured GitHub Issue. Maintainers
      and appointed reviewers decide what is merged. Public users do not edit canonical YAML
      directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={correctionIssueUrl()} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        Suggest a Correction →
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell prose">
    <h2 class="h2">Appointed review</h2>
    <p>
      Founder-appointed reviewers may later propose YAML patches through a platform UI. Those
      proposals must become GitHub pull requests that change <code>context/**/*.yaml</code>.
      Merge remains maintainer-controlled. Automation must not set
      <code>theologically-reviewed</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Local helper for the same patch rules:
      <code>python3 scripts/apply-proposal.py --proposal proposal.json --dry-run</code>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`${SITE.githubUrl}/blob/main/docs/REVIEWER_CORRECTION_WORKFLOW.md`}>Read the reviewer workflow</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
